# five references written as the class or null, and one name that the class does not list: an interface that it implements writes it, optional, as the class or null, and a function stores it through that interface.
# the first late name of a layout takes part in the choice of forms like any slot under its name, but counts in neither sum of "does the cell get smaller": the five narrow slots end at 44 in a cell of 48 (64 with boxed slots).
# behind the laying it is handed what is left by the width of its own form: four bytes are left, it is held to references, four bytes wide, and lies at 44. Boxed it would need a whole word and every object would get an Extension for it.
# with typed slots withheld the five boxed slots fill a cell of 64 and the late name makes it 80.
# -- source: first-late-name-takes-what-a-cell-has-left-by-the-width-of-its-own-form.ts
